NEGATIVE #1, reverted with git, and it is a STRONG REFUTATION rather than an ordinary dead end. The file-local BTN_EDGE macro body `e[var] = lev & (bit);
 hit = 0;
 if (e[var] != 0 && (old & (bit)) == 0) {
 hit = 1;
 }
 e[var] = hit ? e[var] : 0;` was replaced by the logically equivalent and much simpler `e[var] = lev & (bit);
 if ((old & (bit)) != 0) {
 e[var] = 0;
 }` (equivalent because when `lev & bit` is already zero the original also yields zero, so the `e[var] != 0` conjunct is redundant). probe.py reported IMPROVED on `real` (949 -> 802) and this is exactly the trap the metric-discipline section warns about: the instruction count COLLAPSED from 592 to 435 against a target of 611, count distance 19 -> 176, and the multiset EXPLODED from 43t to 214t with target-only +24 b +23 beq +24 bne +45 li +28 cmpwi +16 rlwinm. In other words the target genuinely contains 24 copies of the two-test/`hit`/ternary structure, and the redundant-looking conjunct is load-bearing evidence about the original source. The existing macro shape is hereby CONFIRMED against a measured alternative, not merely assumed. NEGATIVE #2 (inner-block scope), discarded with git: `u32 eD, eC, eA, eB;
 u32 e[24];
 s32 hit;` moved out of the `for (plyr...)` body and into the `if (lev != 0) {` block that is their only reader. Byte-identical object, no frame movement.
